      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nWhen a compressed-tensors scheme requires a newer GPU, `RuntimeError` receives three positional string fragments. Python renders those arguments as a tuple, so users get a noisy message instead of one sentence.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- join the capability error into one string\r\n- add a CPU-only regression test that checks the exception arguments and capability values\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNot applicable; this only changes an unsupported-hardware error path.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot applicable.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format and lint checks pass for the changed files\r\n- [x] Added a registered CPU unit test\r\n- [x] `git diff --check` passes\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\n- focused registered test: `1 passed` in a local CPU-only Python 3.12 environment (compiled `sgl_kernel` imports stubbed; this test exercises config-only logic)\r\n- direct baseline/candidate execution of the actual method body reproduces 3 exception args before the patch and 1 readable arg after it\r\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`: pass\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35609897789](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35609897789)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35609897449](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35609897449)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35609897233](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35609897233)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
